# Skills Loader

## Available Skills

| Skill | File | When to Use |
|---|---|---|
| IDOR | `skills/idor.md` | Testing object-level access controls |
| GraphQL | `skills/graphql.md` | GraphQL endpoint discovery or testing |
| JWT | `skills/jwt.md` | JWT/token validation analysis |
| XSS | `skills/xss.md` | Reflection/stored input testing |
| SSRF | `skills/ssrf.md` | URL-fetch feature analysis |
| Auth Testing | `skills/auth_testing.md` | Session/auth boundary testing |

## Loading Rules

1. When planning a new task node in `attack_graph.json`, check if a matching skill exists.
2. If a skill exists, read it first to follow the methodology.
3. If no skill exists for a test category, create one from `skills/SKILL_TEMPLATE.md` before planning.
4. Skills define: detection heuristics, safe test procedures, evidence checklists, and remediation.
5. Never deviate from the skill's safety boundaries.
